notes:
Tests the critical migration path from anonymous to authenticated.

TEMPMAIL MCP - For signup testing:
- Use `create_email` to get a disposable email address
- Fill signup form with the temp email
- Use `get_messages` to check inbox for magic link
- Use `get_message_detail` to read the magic link email
- Extract the verify URL and navigate to it

Cleanup test users with:
- npx convex run oneTimeMigration:deleteTestUserByEmail '{"email": "<temp-email>"}'

Flow:
1. Anonymous user practices (data stored with visitorId)
2. User signs up with 'Bring progress' checked
3. verify.tsx calls migrateAnonymousData mutation
4. Data now associated with userId
5. localStorage cleared
6. User sees their progress in authenticated dashboard

Test must verify actual data migration, not just localStorage:
```typescript
test('anonymous progress migrates on signup', async ({ page }) => {
  // Practice as anonymous
  await page.goto('/song/baraye');
  await page.click('[data-word="freedom"]');
  await page.click('[data-action="mark-learned"]');

  // Verify localStorage has data
  const visitorId = await page.evaluate(() => 
    localStorage.getItem('songscript_visitor_id')
  );
  expect(visitorId).toBeTruthy();

  // Signup with migration
  await page.goto('/signup');
  await page.fill('[name=email]', testEmail);
  await page.fill('[name=displayName]', 'MigrationTest');
  // checkbox should already be checked
  await page.click('button[type=submit]');

  // Complete magic link flow...

  // Verify dashboard shows migrated data
  await page.goto('/dashboard');
  await expect(page.getByText('1 word')).toBeVisible();

  // Verify localStorage cleared
  const clearedVisitorId = await page.evaluate(() => 
    localStorage.getItem('songscript_visitor_id')
  );
  expect(clearedVisitorId).toBeNull();
});
```
